n still calls for spending to rise 18%, so the plan is not funded through equity.\n- **Pellham's response:** It will cut 2027 transformer orders by about 40%. It will also resize its Q1 2027 transformer tender, currently about C$900M. And it will defer two substation programmes \"until financing improves\". In effect the cutbacks are the funding gap showing up.\n- **Wider market:** The Q3 issuance tracker says two utility share offerings were cut back in size. That points to weak investor appetite across the sector, not a problem at one company.\n- **Norvane Utilities:** It plans 12% higher spending and a C$450M tender in Q2. I found no sign that Norvane has tried to raise equity or been turned away, so its position is untested. It is also much smaller than Pellham.\n\n**Implication:** Equity is not a dependable source for Pellham's 2027 plan. It will probably need debt, which another node found to be shaky for Pellham, or it will cut spending. This is negative for equipment suppliers such as VLTX, which won 60% of the last tender round, mainly through Pellham's Q1 2027 tender.\n\n**Limits:** I did not find the share prices, valuations or the reasons investors gave for the weak demand. I did not read the Norvane or other issuer filings in detail.","ttft_ms":2106,"type":"result","duration_ms":53197,"uuid":"146d98f2-40d6-4867-a66c-c5351aec95dd","ttft_stream_ms":1891,"time_to_request_ms":148,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":5,"system_prompt":7,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":16,"input_hooks":3,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":3,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":70,"init_frame_send":7,"engine_pickup":2,"loop_entry":7,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":0,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":8,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":3,"message_normalization":3,"client_creation":2,"request_build":5},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":98,"time_to_request_cpu_ms"